<title>UK: UK bookmakers cut odds on Conservative victory.</title>
<headline>UK bookmakers cut odds on Conservative victory.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bookmakers William Hill said on Wednesday they had cut the odds on the ruling Conservatives winning the May 1 election to 7-2 from 9-2 following an overnight poll showing the party five points behind Labour.</p>
<p>Labour's odds lengthened to 1-6 from 1-8. The odds on a hung parliament have been cut to 9-2 from 5-1.</p>
</text>
